# Line endings.
#
# Everything under server/ runs on the instance, and a CRLF in a shell script
# breaks its shebang: the kernel looks for an interpreter called "/bin/bash\r".
# The tests run those same scripts on Linux, macOS and Git Bash, so the repo
# stores LF and checks out LF everywhere -- Windows editors have handled LF for
# years, and this is cheaper than debugging a \r that only shows up on the box.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never normalise these.
*.jar  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.tar  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.ico  binary
